This was treated again with a second course of IVIG
with a good response and restoration of mobility.
Conclusions
emur neck fracture is a well-recognized surgical emergency.
This was an unusual and overlooked presentation of an
atraumatic, nonpathological femur neck fracture in a patient
with a neurological disorder and stiffness. Even with widely
accepted therapy with benzodiazepines and baclofen in SPS,
refractory spasms contributed to significant forces on bony
elements leading to a fracture. Primary total hip replacement for
the neck of femur fracture is potentially difficult but reasonable
operative procedure for SPS with neck of femur fracture. n

